{:edb/db-before-t 2098 :edb/db-after-t 2099 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535411 50 #inst "2026-10-08T23:34:31.648Z" 13194139535411 true] [17592186059680 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347781 13194139535411 true] [17592186059681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347774 13194139535411 true] [17592186059681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347788 13194139535411 true] [17592186347774 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347775 13194139535411 true] [17592186347774 1089 "q-104416" 13194139535411 true] [17592186347774 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535411 true] [17592186347774 1100 "Determine the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535411 true] [17592186347774 1113 #uuid "d5749657-28d3-56b8-bb44-5a5929a89f6f" 13194139535411 true] [17592186347774 1145 "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}A=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =(-1)|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2+1)-(1-2)+0 \\\\  & =-3+1+0 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1-4 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{31}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}=\\frac{1}{-2}\\cdot (-5)=\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535411 true] [17592186347775 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347776 13194139535411 true] [17592186347775 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347777 13194139535411 true] [17592186347775 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347778 13194139535411 true] [17592186347775 1000 #edb/ref 